course: dictionary
lesson: 2831
title: Divisible numbers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A number is divisible by another number when you can divide it exactly, with nothing left over. «Most years divisible by 4 are leap years, such as 2024 and 2028.» Here divisible means that 4 fits into the year exactly, with no remainder.
explain: You can check divisibility with simple rules. A number is divisible by 2 if it is even, and by 5 if it ends in 0 or 5. It is divisible by 10 if it ends in 0.
explain: For 3 and 9, add up the digits. If that total is divisible by 3, the number is divisible by 3. If it is divisible by 9, the number is divisible by 9. For example, 36 has digits that add to 9, so 36 is divisible by 9.
fact: Divisible means able to be divided or split into parts with no remainder.
fact: A number is divisible by 2 if it is even, such as 14 or 80.
fact: A number is divisible by 5 if it ends in 0 or 5, and by 10 if it ends in 0.
fact: For 3 and 9, add the digits: if the total is divisible by 3 or by 9, so is the number.
fact: «Most years divisible by 4 are leap years, such as 2024 and 2028.» Phrases to know: divisible by, exactly divisible, not divisible.
exercise: «Most years divisible by 4 are leap years, such as 2024 and 2028.» What does divisible mean here? | Can be counted up to ten | *Can be divided exactly, with no remainder | Has exactly four digits | Is a leap year
exercise: Which number is divisible by 5? | 31 | *40 | 23 | 52
exercise: Is 27 divisible by 3? | No, because 27 is odd | No, because it has two digits | No, because it ends in 7 | *Yes, because 2 + 7 = 9, and 9 is divisible by 3
test: Which number is not divisible by 2? | 46 | 100 | *57 | 18
test: Which number is divisible by 9? | 55 | *81 | 74 | 62
exam: Is 45 divisible by 2? | Yes, because 4 + 5 = 9 | *No, because 45 is odd, so it is not even | Yes, because it ends in 5
